 "subs": [
  {
   "a": 16.34,
   "b": 20.225,
   "text": "Long ago, we did not know how the world worked."
  },
  {
   "a": 20.939999999999998,
   "b": 25.026,
   "text": "But we had already begun to look for our place in it."
  },
  {
   "a": 30.939999999999998,
   "b": 38.158,
   "text": "The ancients said: heaven is round, the earth is square, and we stand between them."
  },
  {
   "a": 38.388,
   "b": 43.793,
   "text": "Heaven, earth, and humankind — the three powers of the world."
  },
  {
   "a": 44.253,
   "b": 48.291,
   "text": "In legend, Nüwa shaped us from yellow clay."
  },
  {
   "a": 48.853,
   "b": 52.729,
   "text": "In the Bible, God made us in His own image."
  },
  {
   "a": 56.053,
   "b": 60.677,
   "text": "Nearly every civilization placed us at the center of the world."
  },
  {
   "a": 61.247,
   "b": 66.401,
   "text": "In the second century, Ptolemy placed the Earth at the center of the universe."
  },
  {
   "a": 67.031,
   "b": 70.947,
   "text": "That picture lasted nearly fourteen hundred years."
  },
  {
   "a": 73.537,
   "b": 78.549,
   "text": "In 1543, Copernicus gave the center to the Sun."
  },
  {
   "a": 80.43700000000001,
   "b": 86.807,
   "text": "In 1610, through his telescope, Galileo saw moons circling Jupiter."
  },
  {
   "a": 87.037,
   "b": 90.341,
   "text": "Not everything in the sky turned around us."
  },
  {
   "a": 91.061,
   "b": 96.097,
   "text": "The Sun is just one of hundreds of billions of stars in our galaxy."
  },
  {
   "a": 97.32700000000001,
   "b": 101.528,
   "text": "And our galaxy is just one of hundreds of billions more."
  },
  {
   "a": 103.26100000000001,
   "b": 114.749,
   "text": "If the 13.8-billion-year history of the universe were compressed into a single year, everything we call civilization would fill only its final seconds."
  },
  {
   "a": 116.229,
   "b": 122.549,
   "text": "In 1990, from six billion kilometers away, Voyager 1 looked back."
  },
  {
   "a": 123.379,
   "b": 126.679,
   "text": "The Earth was only a pale blue dot."
  },
  {
   "a": 130.34900000000002,
   "b": 134.805,
   "text": "We had lost the center. At least we still had our origin."
  },
  {
   "a": 135.13500000000002,
   "b": 145.377,
   "text": "We believed all things stood on a great ladder: God, angels, humankind — and below us, beasts, plants, and stones."
  },
  {
   "a": 145.707,
   "b": 149.813,
   "text": "We stood near the top, a single step from God."
  },
  {
   "a": 149.933,
   "b": 155.064,
   "text": "In 1859, Darwin published On the Origin of Species."
  },
  {
   "a": 155.38400000000001,
   "b": 158.667,
   "text": "The ladder fell, and grew into a tree."
  },
  {
   "a": 161.984,
   "b": 170.671,
   "text": "A fish's fin, a bat's wing, a whale's flipper, a human hand — the same bones, rearranged."
  },
  {
   "a": 171.101,
   "b": 176.736,
   "text": "Nearly all life is built of cells, and written in the same genetic code."
  },
  {
   "a": 177.366,
   "b": 187.009,
   "text": "Our DNA is nearly ninety-nine percent the same as a chimpanzee's. Six or seven million years ago, we shared a common ancestor."
  },
  {
   "a": 187.779,
   "b": 190.836,
   "text": "We were not placed in this world apart."
  },
  {
   "a": 191.26600000000002,
   "b": 194.983,
   "text": "We are one ordinary branch on the tree of life."
  },
  {
   "a": 198.653,
   "b": 205.103,
   "text": "Stripped of place and origin, we retreated to our last stronghold: the mind."
  },
  {
   "a": 205.433,
   "b": 209.733,
   "text": "Descartes wrote: I think, therefore I am."
  },
  {
   "a": 210.06300000000002,
   "b": 213.444,
   "text": "Reason became the mark of what makes us human."
  },
  {
   "a": 213.364,
   "b": 219.392,
   "text": "Then we found that thought is electricity and chemistry, flowing between neurons."
  },
  {
   "a": 221.064,
   "b": 226.09,
   "text": "And then, with our own hands, we began to build things that think."
  },
  {
   "a": 226.24,
   "b": 231.89,
   "text": "In 1950, Turing asked a question: can machines think?"
  },
  {
   "a": 232.55,
   "b": 237.764,
   "text": "Forty-seven years later, Deep Blue defeated the world chess champion."
  },
  {
   "a": 238.084,
   "b": 244.505,
   "text": "Nineteen years after that, AlphaGo played a move almost none of us would ever have played."
  },
  {
   "a": 245.165,
   "b": 250.016,
   "text": "Four years later, AlphaFold predicted how proteins fold."
  },
  {
   "a": 250.251,
   "b": 255.621,
   "text": "Two years after that, it began to speak with us, in our own language."
  },
  {
   "a": 255.956,
   "b": 261.046,
   "text": "The gaps shrank from decades, to years, to months."
  },
  {
   "a": 261.366,
   "b": 265.348,
   "text": "Now they write, paint, code, and reason —"
  },
  {
   "a": 265.27799999999996,
   "b": 267.488,
   "text": "and answer our questions."
  },
  {
   "a": 267.41799999999995,
   "b": 271.361,
   "text": "Work that takes us days, they finish in minutes."
  },
  {
   "a": 271.34099999999995,
   "b": 278.35,
   "text": "Writing, coding, even making films — at many tasks, they now outperform most of us."
  },
  {
   "a": 278.58,
   "b": 284.644,
   "text": "They still fall short of the very best of us. But that gap is not beyond closing."
  },
  {
   "a": 285.034,
   "b": 291.732,
   "text": "Even this film — its animation, its music, its narration — was made by AI."
  },
  {
   "a": 309.892,
   "b": 314.579,
   "text": "Each time, we thought we had found the last reason we were special."
  },
  {
   "a": 315.109,
   "b": 318.821,
   "text": "And each time, knowledge gave it back to nature."
  },
  {
   "a": 318.71099999999996,
   "b": 322.148,
   "text": "Perhaps science has only ever done one thing:"
  },
  {
   "a": 322.77799999999996,
   "b": 325.825,
   "text": "it has brought us down from the altar."
  },
  {
   "a": 328.311,
   "b": 331.663,
   "text": "We are not at the center of the universe,"
  },
  {
   "a": 331.993,
   "b": 334.393,
   "text": "not at the summit of creation,"
  },
  {
   "a": 334.72299999999996,
   "b": 337.8,
   "text": "and not even the only things that think."
  },
  {
   "a": 338.65999999999997,
   "b": 340.602,
   "text": "We are ordinary."
  }
 ],
